    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (3/3 tests, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I did\n\nThe repo already had an `AddressNormalizer` component (lower-casing, whitespace-collapsing) wired into household duplicate detection and the shared household id. I extended it to meet the new spec:\n\n**`AddressNormalizer.normalize`** \u2014 now trims, collapses whitespace, **upper-cases**, and **expands abbreviations token-by-token** (`ST\u2192STREET`, `RD\u2192ROAD`, `AVE\u2192AVENUE`). A null/blank address canonicalises to the empty string. The expansion is per-token, so a word like `STREET` isn't further altered (idempotent).\n\n**`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 on create it now:\n- normalizes the incoming address,\n- **rejects it with 400 if blank after normalization** (required-field check),\n- **stores the normalized form** on the owner (`owner.setAddress(address)`), so it is what gets persisted and returned.\n\nBecause the normalized address is stored before the household checks run, both `isHouseholdInUse` (duplicate detection) and `householdId` (shared household id) compare on the normalized form \u2014 they call `addressNormalizer.normalize` on both the candidate and each existing owner, and re-normalizing an already-normalized value is idempotent.\n\nThe three acceptance tests confirm the behavior:\n- `\"  12  main  st \"` \u2192 stored/returned as `\"12 MAIN STREET\"`\n- `\"7 elm ave\"` \u2192 `\"7 ELM AVENUE\"`\n- `\"   \"` \u2192 400 Bad Request",
